\text{possession} &\longrightarrow \text{pleasure sustained}.\end{aligned}

p.src:
When this movement is blocked, it does not remain harmless. Krishnamurti names the sequence directly: $\text{thwarted pleasure}
\longrightarrow
\text{frustration}
\longrightarrow
\text{anger, jealousy, violence}.$ The notation should be read as a disciplined reminder of the spoken order, not as a mechanical theory of behavior. The point is that pursued pleasure, when denied, becomes conflict.

