p.src:
The distinction can be recorded as $\begin{aligned}
\text{cultivated capacity} &\sim \text{time},\\
\text{perception} &\not\sim \text{time}.\end{aligned}$ This is a conceptual notation, not physics notation. It preserves the difference in the transcript: practice may require duration, but perception is not perfected at the end of practice.

